# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_per_push.py" "COCHANGE PER-PUSH GATE: PASS" "co-change per-push increment (keep the empirical-coupling signal CURRENT on every push, content-free, no clone)" "co-change PER-PUSH: keep the co-change (logical-coupling) signal CURRENT on every push WITHOUT a clone, with the EXACT precision discipline of the full-history batch path. co-change is SEEDED by a full backfill (a blobless clone of git history), so between backfills the live per-push path refreshes the structural graph but leaves co-change STALE -- exactly when (high-velocity / AI-era) coupling is forming. The fix folds each push's commits into the co-change counters incrementally; a webhook push payload's commits[] each carry their added/modified/removed file lists = the content-free co-change input, so NO clone is needed. MEASURE-FIRST proves the load-bearing property -- EQUIVALENCE: folding a set of commits' changed-file lists incrementally counts BYTE-IDENTICALLY to the batch _git_log_commits->fold over the SAME commits (one shared fold_commits + emit_pairs underneath both paths -> no second copy of the giant-commit skip / support floor / lift / 0%-not-evaluated rule that could drift). Proven on a REAL git history (clone path == per-push increment path emit byte-identical pairs) AND synthetic commit sets: (a) increment over the same commits == batch; (b) ASSOCIATIVITY (N pushes folded one-by-one == one batch over all -> streaming is exact); (c) GIANT-COMMIT SKIP survives the per-push path (a 50-file commit mints no pairs); (d) RE-DELIVERY without dedup double-counts (so caller sha-dedup is REQUIRED) and a sha-deduped redelivery is a true NO-OP (idempotent-safe); (e) FAIL-OPEN -- the content-free push_commit_filesets reader NEVER raises on a malformed/injected payload (the increment is the advisory 2nd signal: a payload it can't read yields no increment, never a crash that drops the structural verdict); (f) SEED reconstruction from stored pairs + a push increments the counters by exactly the push (the HONEST all-time-additive trade: the increment accumulates on the last stored signal; the periodic re-backfill stays the source of truth). content-free end to end (paths + counts only -- no body, message, or author). git only; NO Postgres" "co-change per-push: incremental commit-fold counts byte-identically to the batch (shared fold_commits/emit_pairs), proven on a real history; giant-commit skip survives, re-delivery dedup required+effective, fail-open reader never raises, content-free, no clone" 24
